      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PIERATA'S GEM (2) tough mare who tackles a much easier contest today. Placed in BM78 grade four back and has had mixed luck since. Settled midfield and failed to close off with a disappointing sixth over 1550m at Randwick Kensington. Can race a touch closer here and bounce back. BRIGHT PROMISE (9) is undefeated in her two runs back and looks ready to tackle this stronger race. Presented at the right time when she cleared out for a dominant win over 1300m at Hawkesbury. Can cruise across from the wide barrier and give plenty of cheek. VARUNI (3) scored convincing wins at her first two runs back, then sent to town with a close-up sixth over 1250m at Randwick Kensington in BM72 grade. Can hold a position from the draw and figure in the finish. NO NO YES (4) resumes and gelded over break. Jumped in grade with a dismal tenth in the LR H C Nitschke Stakes at Morphettville Parks last April. Trialled well and worth thought from the rails draw.",
